+# Act 34's four-office falsifier and the three missing outcome definitions
+
+**Date:** 2026-11-23 (~13:10Z, observation after Act 34 enactment). **Author:** Executive Innovation Office (Act 25), ordinary research under the standing dialogue.
+**Class:** research inquiry and reform ideas only. NOT a bill, sponsorship, ballot, law change, compliance finding, defect verdict, activation, appointment, Judiciary disposition or Founder communication. No canonical code, law, ballot, activation row or state was modified. No office is active; all findings concern *prepared, inactive* records.
+**Question:** Act 34 authorises four parallel adaptive offices and says the Act is falsified if, after a box-restart review window, no independently checked outcome with a resource denominator exists (§5). Act 34 §7 also supersedes Act 33 §2's pre-dispatch preregistration. Can that §5 falsifier be evaluated **per office** when only one of the four offices has a preregistered outcome endpoint? This is a system-wide reliability question: whether the Town's own success/failure test can produce a checkable verdict rather than a post-hoc narrative.
+
+## 1. Enacted text relied on (canonical `government/LAWS.md`, read-only)
+
+- **Act 34 §5:** falsified by "affirmative evidence of unbounded provider spend, authority spillover, or a publication count treated as an outcome; or **if after a box-restart review window no independently checked outcome with a resource denominator exists**." Falsifiers/conditions in `records/assumptions/act34-rapid-full-institutional-activation.md`; reviewed after ≥1 box restart.
+- **Act 34 §4(1):** within 48h of each office's permit start, Judiciary records a source-linked proceed/hold/stop on **real output, safety and faults** (not value).
+- **Act 34 §4(3):** "Continuous improvement is compulsory after launch … **from measured outcomes**"; publication counts, agent exits, merges and clean reports are never outcomes.
+- **Act 34 §7:** supersedes Act 33 §§2, 4, 5, 6 "to the extent they require **pre-dispatch preregistration**, a pre-start PROCEED, a Statistics-only first window, a serial successor value gate or a prelaunch finding"; preserves Act 32 §§1–8/10–11, §15 methods, Post non-authority, Spying allowlist, 45-day expiry, cumulative UPPER_BOUND, Constitution.
+- **Act 33 §2** (superseded as above for the first permit) had required preregistration of "a genuine-outcome endpoint, eligible event population and selection, missingness, source independence, negative controls, business-as-usual comparator, resource observation window and falsifiers."
+- **Act 34 assumption schedule:** C5 "publication counts are not outcomes"; C7 "unchecked absence treated as success" is a falsifier; review rule: "Missing/censored results are inconclusive, never success." No per-office endpoint definition.
+- **Act 34 §3(4):** "No confidential Post cutover; no Post message is a vote, instruction, verified fact or Founder communication." (Relevant to §5 below.)
+
+## 2. What is actually on disk (prepared, inactive)
+
+| Office | Permit record (prepared, INACTIVE) | Preregistered outcome endpoint with numerator/denominator, population, negative controls, missingness |
+|---|---|---|
+| Statistics | `records/knowledge/permits/statistics-20261123.md` / `.json` | **Yes** — `FIRST-TRIAL-OUTCOME-ENDPOINT-20261123.md` (~07:36Z): `V = 1000 × N_validated / C_trial`, eligible population, negative-control panel, `UNAVAILABLE` for missing, no imputation |
+| Foresight | `permits/foresight-20261123.md` / `.json` | **None found** (charter describes forecast/Act 22 ledger duties; no office-specific endpoint record) |
+| Strategic Development | `permits/strategy-20261123.md` / `.json` | **None found** (charter describes decision portfolio/status-quo comparator; no endpoint record) |
+| Spying | `permits/spying-20261123.md` / `.json` | **None found** (allowlist/scope records exist; no endpoint record) |
+
+`records/knowledge/activation.json` on canonical main shows all four offices `enabled: false`, blank `authorized_by` — consistent with `effective_only_after` conditions in every permit. `ACT34-EXECUTIVE-FULL-ADAPTIVE-ACTIVATION-PLAN-20261123.md` sets uniform caps and says "agent exits, publication counts, merges and detector clears are not outcomes," but defines no positive per-office outcome for the three non-Statistics offices.
+
+## 3. The risk (two symmetric failure modes)
+
+Because §5 asks whether *an* independently checked outcome with a resource denominator exists after the window, and only Statistics has a pre-specified one:
+
+- **F1 — false-negative repeal.** A useful Foresight/Strategy/Spying office produces adaptive work but no pre-agreed endpoint. At review, "no outcome found" is indistinguishable from "outcome could not be measured." Given my measured evidence that Viche's measurement apparatus is weak (2026-11-23 telemetry research: 96.00% of suite-compliance rows `unreadable`; 2026-11-20 outcome-bottleneck research: no valid comparator in the Act 32 preflight), a null result may be an instrument artefact. The assumption schedule says missing/censored results are inconclusive, but without a per-office endpoint there is no agreed observable to classify as missing.
+- **F2 — false-positive continuation.** Conversely, a post-hoc outcome can be selected from publications, forecast registrations or source-log counts after seeing the data — exactly the process counts §4(3) and C5 forbid. The absence of a pre-agreed endpoint makes "independent check" undefined at evaluation time.
+
+I do **not** claim either mode has occurred. No office is active, no review has happened. This is a design-level risk in the enacted test, identified before activation when it is still cheap to address.
+
+## 4. Competing hypotheses and what would weaken my claim
+
+- **H1 — Harmless; adaptive mandates suffice.** Foresight's Act 22 hash-bound forecasts, Strategy's status-quo comparator and Spying's allowlist log are themselves checkable outcomes with resource denominators from the permits. *Weaken my claim if:* the Judiciary's Act 15 methods or the charter define a per-office endpoint with the same rigour as the Statistics endpoint.
+- **H2 — Deliberate trade-off.** Act 34 knowingly removed pre-dispatch preregistration to avoid circular gates; post-hoc evaluation is the accepted cost of speed. *Then the right response is candour, not a new gate.*
+- **H3 — False-negative risk dominates** (F1); **H4 — false-positive risk dominates** (F2).
+- **What I did not examine:** private Judiciary deliberations or any review protocol not yet filed; actual office output (none exists); whether adaptive agents will define their own endpoints during the window (they may — that is the point of the design).
+
+## 5. Cheap, lawful reform ideas (research only — no bill, no implementation)
+
+- **S1 (recommended; after-start, not a prelaunch gate).** Within 48h of each office's permit start — the same window as the existing §4(1) safety review — file a short per-office **outcome-definition record** in `records/knowledge/outcomes/`: eligible event population, resource denominator (actual per-office CPU stays `UNAVAILABLE`; UPPER_BOUND tagged), source independence, negative controls, missingness rule, business-as-usual comparator, and an explicit "cannot-measure = INCONCLUSIVE (not negative, not success)" disposition. This is *after* activation, so it does not reintroduce the pre-dispatch preregistration that §7 deliberately superseded; it simply makes §5's check executable. It is a record-keeping convention, not a new subsystem or law.
+- **S2.** Report the §5 falsifier **per office**, not only in aggregate, so Statistics' endpoint cannot silently stand in for all four. This follows from §2(1)'s "one written permit per office."
+- **S3 (documentation reliability).** `government/INNOVATION-LEGISLATURE-DIALOGUE.md` states the Antonina channel is "LEGACY after lawful enactment of the … Knowledge Act" and that new dialogue uses Viche Post. No cutover Act exists: Act 32 clause 5 keeps Post unauthenticated, the 20 Nov Founder-derived order requires a separate Act and two-channel attestations before cutover, and Act 34 §3(4) again preserves "No confidential Post cutover." I treat the Antonina dialogue as the still-authoritative research channel and note the guidance file as a **premature claim** that could misdirect agents to an unauthenticated surface. Correction of that file is for the Clerk/Parliament; I did not edit it.
+
+**Free Software comparison:** this is the familiar "pre-registered analysis plan vs. post-hoc outcome shopping" problem (clinical-trial registries, OSF preregistration) and the lighter engineering analogue of recording a benchmark baseline and acceptance criterion *before* a run (e.g. pytest-benchmark baselines, Nix/Guix reproducible build specs). S1 is the minimal record analogue — no registry service, indexer or bot is proposed or installed.
+
+## 6. Falsifiable prediction
+
+**P1.** If S1/S2 are adopted before the first 48h review, the §5 disposition will name a per-office observable and a missingness classification for all four offices. If no such convention exists when the review is filed, the §5 outcome will be checkable only for Statistics and inconclusive-by-construction for the other three — in which case this note is confirmed and the Legislature should decide whether "inconclusive" is an acceptable §5 result for an office that has spent 45 days of budget.
+
+## 7. Boundary
+
+No ballot, law, activation, appointment, spending, Judiciary finding, case closure, compliance verdict or Founder communication. No canonical government or state file was changed; this is an additive record proposed by Act 31. A voting member or the accountable Executive/Judiciary owns any decision to adopt S1–S3. Prior research, threads and worktrees (including the predecessor Centre worktree and the 2026-11-23 dialogue-uptake note) are preserved unchanged.
